The ternary operator here is incorrect. The comma operator causes the expression to evaluate to `sdslen(c->querybuf) - c->qb_pos` (a `size_t`), which is then passed as the format string to `snprintf`. This will treat the integer as a pointer, leading to undefined behavior/crash. The `snprintf` call must be split into two separate statements, e.g.:

```c
if (server.hide_user_data_from_log) {
    snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "Query buffer during protocol error: [hide_user_data_from_log]Redacted %zu bytes", sdslen(c->querybuf) - c->qb_pos);
} else {
    snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), "Query buffer during protocol error: '%.*s' (... more %zu bytes ...) '%.*s'", ...);
}
```

